HST Office: the native boxes of the ribbon fit its rows on gtk3.

GTK draws a combo box, entry or spin button at its own height whatever height vcl gives it. Adwaita's boxes
ask 31-34 px (the theme's vertical padding and min-height), the ribbon's rows are 24 px, so the toolbox clipped
their bottom: the fill style and line width boxes of the picture and shape tabs at 100 %, Table Design's fill
style at 125 % (GDK_DPI_SCALE 1.25), the frame's lower edge gone and the text cut. The gtk3 backend now gives the
native widgets of an item window in the ribbon (vcl/HstRibbonRow.hxx: a NotebookBar above it) the style class
"hst-ribbon-row", whose combo boxes, entries and spin buttons drop their vertical padding and minimum height:
the box is its text line and its frame, which fits 24 px at 100 % and 125 %. Rows keep their height; toolbars,
the sidebar and dialogs keep the theme's boxes; Windows and macOS are unchanged.

- include/vcl/HstRibbonRow.hxx, vcl/source/control/HstRibbonRow.cxx (new), vcl/Library_vcl.mk;
  vcl/unx/gtk3/gtkinst.cxx (CreateInterimBuilder), vcl/unx/gtk3/gtkdata.cxx (the CSS).

License: new HST files LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary; the hooks stay under the upstream files' license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_ribbon_gtk3_boxes_fit_rows.py; tests/runtime/collect-ribbon-v3-dumps.py with
check-ribbon-v3-dumps.py on Linux gtk3 at 100 % and 125 % (box_clip and label_cut).

